+| `MIP_GOMORY_MORE` | 20 | On a model whose objective step finds implied integers, and unless the rounds are set, the root's Gomory rounds go past `MIP_CUT_ROUNDS`, up to this many: a round runs while the one before lifted the bound by `MIP_GOMORY_MORE_STALL` and its cuts held at most `MIP_GOMORY_MORE_NZ` times the model's nonzeros. `MIP_MIR_MORE`'s value. `assign1-5-8` stops at the stall after 8 rounds, its root from 189.80 to 192.30 and its bound at 1e10 from 197.32–197.52 to 199.04–199.36 over five null readings; MIPLIB 3, where only `misc03` and `misc07` have implied integers and their first round lifts nothing, reads 0.996x (`bench/measurements/02-483/`) |
+| `MIP_GOMORY_MORE_STALL` | 1e-4 | The share of (1 + \|bound\|) a round must lift the bound by for the next Gomory round to run; `MIP_MIR_MORE_STALL`'s value. `assign1-5-8`'s second to seventh rounds lift 5.7e-3 to 3.1e-4 of it and its eighth 8.6e-5. Not swept |
+| `MIP_GOMORY_MORE_NZ` | 10 | The most nonzeros a round's cuts may hold, as a multiple of the model's, for the next Gomory round to run. `assign1-5-8`'s rounds hold 3.5 to 4.9 times its nonzeros; `csched007`'s first holds 18 and each after it 23 to 41: with five rounds a node costs 2.8 times as much and its bound at 1e10 falls from 306 to 302, and under the stall alone its root takes the whole 1e10 and reads 296 (`bench/measurements/02-483/`). Not swept |
 | `MIP_CUT_AWAY` | 0.01 | A basic integer column is cut only when its fraction lies in `[AWAY, 1 - AWAY]`, since the cut divides by the fraction and its complement. Balas, Ceria, Cornuejols and Natraj's bound. Not swept |
 | `MIP_CUT_DROP` | 1e-9 | A coefficient below `DROP` times the cut's largest is folded into the right-hand side through its column's bound, which keeps the cut valid; kept when that bound is infinite. Not swept |
 | `MIP_CUT_SLACK` | 1e-15 | How far a cut's right-hand side is pulled back, in units of its span `1 + \|rhs\| + Σ_j \|a_j\| max(1, \|l_j\|, \|u_j\|)`. A rounded-up side can cut off the integer points on it and make a feasible model read infeasible; pulling back only keeps points. Over 20000 generated models checked by enumeration it removes every false infeasible. 1e-15 covers one rounding step; 1e-11 loosened the bound enough to lose `misc03` |
